  {
   "n": 8,
   "type": "MCQ",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "",
   "html": "<p>An $XY$ flip-flop operates as indicated by the following table :<br>\n$$\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|}<br>\n\\hline \\text { Input(X) } &amp; \\text { Input(Y) } &amp; \\text { Current State } &amp; \\text { Next State } \\\\<br>\n\\hline X &amp; Y &amp; &amp; \\\\<br>\n\\hline 0 &amp; 0 &amp; Q &amp; 1 \\\\<br>\n\\hline 0 &amp; 1 &amp; Q &amp; \\overline{Q} \\\\<br>\n\\hline 1 &amp; 1 &amp; Q &amp; 0 \\\\<br>\n\\hline 1 &amp; 0 &amp; Q &amp; Q \\\\<br>\n\\hline<br>\n\\end{array}$$<br>\nWhich of the following expresses the next state in terms of the $X$ and $Y$ inputs and the current state $Q ?$</p>",
   "paragraph": null,
   "options": [
    {
     "key": "A",
     "html": "<p>$(\\overline{X} \\wedge \\overline{Q}) \\vee(\\overline{Y} \\wedge Q)$</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "B",
     "html": "<p>$(\\overline{Y} \\wedge \\overline{Q}) \\vee(\\overline{X} \\wedge Q)$</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "C",
     "html": "<p>$(X \\wedge \\overline{Q}) \\vee(Y \\wedge Q)$</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "D",
     "html": "<p>$(\\overline{Y} \\wedge \\overline{Q}) \\vee(\\overline{Q} \\wedge X)$</p>"
    }
   ],
   "answer": [
    "A"
   ],
   "natRange": null,
   "answerText": "A",
   "marks": {
    "pos": 2,
    "neg": 0.6667
   },
   "solution": "<p><strong>Answer:</strong> A</p><p><a href=\"https://gateoverflow.in/376234\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Official discussion page</a></p>"
